# Routing And Entrypoints

Reference `src/routes/README.md` for routing constraints.

## Route file policy

- Export only `Route` via `createFileRoute`. No components, no business logic.
- Heavy logic goes to `actions`, `widgets`, `features`, `entrypoints`, `shared`, or `lib`.
- Use `component: MyComponent` pointing to an entrypoint component.

## Route layout groups

```
src/routes/
├── __root.tsx                    # Root with RouterContext (queryClient, sessionData)
├── _auth/                        # Unauthenticated pages (sign-in, verify-otp)
├── _with-auth/                   # Auth guard — redirects to sign-in if no session
│   ├── _with-subscription/       # Requires active subscription
│   └── _without-subscription/    # Auth but no subscription
└── _without-auth/                # Redirects authenticated users
```

## RouterContext

Available in `beforeLoad` and `loader`:
```typescript
type RouterContext = { queryClient: QueryClient; sessionData?: GetSession200 };
```

## Patterns

```typescript
// Minimal route file
export const Route = createFileRoute("/_with-auth/_with-subscription/my-page")({
  validateSearch: zodValidator(searchSchema),
  beforeLoad: async ({ context }) => {
    await context.queryClient.ensureQueryData(getSomethingQueryOptions());
  },
  component: MyPageComponent,  // from src/entrypoints/my-page/component.tsx
});
```

```typescript
// Search params validation
import { zodValidator } from "@tanstack/zod-adapter";
import { z } from "@/lib/zod";

const searchSchema = z.object({ q: z.string().optional(), page: z.number().optional() });
```

## Generation workflow

- Route tree: `src/codegen/router/route-tree.gen.ts` — never edit manually.
- After any route file changes: `pnpm router:generate`.
- During active route development: `pnpm router:watch`.
